{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39649022",
      "title": "Making Components Reusable with Props [Core Concept]",
      "sourceHash": "a5fbd099a0a851bff83b156867f1d79b4e3b006260bc3a1224521102bdade518",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.24,
          "end": 1.53,
          "en": "So now that we know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.53,
          "end": 4.2,
          "en": "how we can output dynamic data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.2,
          "end": 8.28,
          "en": "let's go back to components and what we can do with those.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.28,
          "end": 12.03,
          "en": "Because one of the main advantages of components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.03,
          "end": 14.25,
          "en": "is that they are reusable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.25,
          "end": 16.92,
          "en": "we can, for example, use this header component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.92,
          "end": 19.08,
          "en": "as often as we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.08,
          "end": 21.63,
          "en": "And if we do that we, of course, see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.63,
          "end": 23.733,
          "en": "multiple headers on this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.63,
          "end": 28.14,
          "en": "But, of course, here for the header component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.14,
          "end": 30.6,
          "en": "reusing it is possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.6,
          "end": 33.54,
          "en": "but doesn't really make a lot of sense, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.54,
          "end": 36.3,
          "en": "and that's also quite normal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.3,
          "end": 39.21,
          "en": "You will also often build components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.21,
          "end": 42.93,
          "en": "which might be reusable in theory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.93,
          "end": 46.95,
          "en": "but indeed are only meant to be used once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.95,
          "end": 48.63,
          "en": "But it's also quite common",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.63,
          "end": 52.89,
          "en": "to have components that should be reused multiple times.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.89,
          "end": 56.79,
          "en": "For example, here, these core concept items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.79,
          "end": 61.79,
          "en": "here we might wanna build one single core concept component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.34,
          "end": 65.79,
          "en": "which can then be reused four times",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.79,
          "end": 69.03,
          "en": "for these four different key concepts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.03,
          "end": 71.07,
          "en": "but every time we're using it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.07,
          "end": 74.78999999999999,
          "en": "it should be used with different data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.78999999999999,
          "end": 79.35,
          "en": "Just as you can define a normal JavaScript function once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.35,
          "end": 81.75,
          "en": "and then use it multiple times,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.75,
          "end": 84.90299999999999,
          "en": "thanks to this concept of working with parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.86,
          "end": 88.62,
          "en": "So just as you can build and reuse",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.62,
          "end": 91.65,
          "en": "JavaScript functions with different data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.65,
          "end": 94.44,
          "en": "we also might want to build and reuse",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.44,
          "end": 99.09,
          "en": "certain React Components with different input data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.09,
          "end": 103.83,
          "en": "And that's why React offers another crucial concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.83,
          "end": 108.18,
          "en": "that's related to components called props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.18,
          "end": 111.24000000000001,
          "en": "And this props concept is all about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.24000000000001,
          "end": 115.28999999999999,
          "en": "being able to pass data into components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.28999999999999,
          "end": 118.25999999999999,
          "en": "and to then use that data in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.25999999999999,
          "end": 120.69,
          "en": "And for that here in our project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.69,
          "end": 124.05,
          "en": "for the moment still in this app.jsx file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.05,
          "end": 126.27,
          "en": "though that will change soon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.27,
          "end": 128.82,
          "en": "we can add a new component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.82,
          "end": 132.42,
          "en": "maybe a component function called CoreConcept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.42,
          "end": 136.023,
          "en": "since it should be about outputting core concept data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.07,
          "end": 141.42000000000002,
          "en": "And then here I want to output a list item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.42000000000002,
          "end": 145.383,
          "en": "where I have an image with a source and an alt tag,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.7,
          "end": 150.27,
          "en": "where I have an h3 tag with some title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 150.27,
          "end": 153.423,
          "en": "and a paragraph with some description.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 154.26,
          "end": 157.29,
          "en": "And, of course, the goal is to not just have this title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 157.29,
          "end": 159.54,
          "en": "and description placeholder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.54,
          "end": 163.68,
          "en": "but to instead have actual data that's different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.68,
          "end": 167.76,
          "en": "every time this core concept component gets used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.76,
          "end": 170.37,
          "en": "So now with that component defined here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.37,
          "end": 172.23,
          "en": "we can go to the app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.23,
          "end": 176.43,
          "en": "and here in the main area I'll add a new section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 176.43,
          "end": 179.52,
          "en": "with an idea of core concepts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 179.52,
          "end": 183.24,
          "en": "and I'm only adding that for styling purposes here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.24,
          "end": 186.09,
          "en": "because in this index.ccs file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 186.09,
          "end": 189.243,
          "en": "there is a core concepts ID selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.68,
          "end": 193.83,
          "en": "So make sure you get this ID right",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.83,
          "end": 197.13,
          "en": "to get the same styling as I have it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.13,
          "end": 199.89,
          "en": "And then I'll move to h2 tag in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 199.89,
          "end": 204.24,
          "en": "and maybe give it a text of Core Concepts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204.24,
          "end": 207.09,
          "en": "and below that add an unordered list;",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.09,
          "end": 210.48,
          "en": "and now my goal is to use this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.48,
          "end": 213,
          "en": "newly added core concept component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 213,
          "end": 216.273,
          "en": "here in this unordered list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 217.32,
          "end": 220.95,
          "en": "And the goal, of course, is to use that multiple times,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 220.95,
          "end": 225.75,
          "en": "but every time I'm using it I wanna pass in different data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 225.75,
          "end": 230.28,
          "en": "And thanks to this props concept, that's super easy to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 230.28,
          "end": 233.1,
          "en": "you can simply add custom attributes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 233.1,
          "end": 235.65,
          "en": "to your custom components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 235.65,
          "end": 238.11,
          "en": "and since these are your components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 238.11,
          "end": 240.48,
          "en": "it's also entirely up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 240.48,
          "end": 244.59,
          "en": "which attributes you wanna set on those components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 244.59,
          "end": 249.24,
          "en": "so those attribute names are also entirely up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 249.24,
          "end": 253.02,
          "en": "And here I'll start by adding a title attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 253.02,
          "end": 256.02,
          "en": "and I'll set it equal to a value of components here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 256.02,
          "end": 258.663,
          "en": "for this first usage of core concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 260.91,
          "end": 265.91,
          "en": "And I'll add a description attribute, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 266.34,
          "end": 269.37,
          "en": "though, in React we actually call that a prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 269.37,
          "end": 271.23,
          "en": "because that concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 271.23,
          "end": 275.37,
          "en": "of configuring components is called props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 275.37,
          "end": 277.53,
          "en": "And for this description prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 277.53,
          "end": 282.153,
          "en": "we could say the core UI building block, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 283.47,
          "end": 286.08,
          "en": "And last but not least, we can add an image here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 286.08,
          "end": 289.98,
          "en": "and here I actually wanna set this to a dynamic value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 289.98,
          "end": 292.11,
          "en": "because I want to import that image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 292.11,
          "end": 295.59000000000003,
          "en": "just as I showed it to you in the last lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 295.59000000000003,
          "end": 298.08,
          "en": "So here we can now import the components image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 298.08,
          "end": 302.373,
          "en": "from ./assets/component.png,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 303.72,
          "end": 307.5,
          "en": "and with that import added we can use components image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 307.5,
          "end": 309.54,
          "en": "this variable here in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 309.54,
          "end": 311.76,
          "en": "and use that as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 311.76,
          "end": 316.023,
          "en": "for this image prop written like this now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 317.22,
          "end": 318.87,
          "en": "And that's also important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 318.87,
          "end": 322.02,
          "en": "you can really pass all kinds of values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 322.02,
          "end": 324.9,
          "en": "as values for your props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 324.9,
          "end": 327.99,
          "en": "You can pass strings, as I'm doing this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 327.99,
          "end": 330.18,
          "en": "but you can also pass numbers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 330.18,
          "end": 333.03,
          "en": "like the number two if you needed that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 333.03,
          "end": 336.3,
          "en": "you can pass in objects or arrays,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 336.3,
          "end": 339.18,
          "en": "really whatever you need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 339.18,
          "end": 341.49,
          "en": "Here I'm passing this data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 341.49,
          "end": 345.81,
          "en": "and with that data being passed to this component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 345.81,
          "end": 348.903,
          "en": "we now just have to accept and use it there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 349.95,
          "end": 352.92,
          "en": "Now in normal JavaScript functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 352.92,
          "end": 355.74,
          "en": "you would simply add one or more parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 355.74,
          "end": 360.74,
          "en": "to accept input values and to then use these input values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 361.11,
          "end": 363.72,
          "en": "When working with React component functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 363.72,
          "end": 365.49,
          "en": "it's pretty much the same,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 365.49,
          "end": 369.39,
          "en": "but you only accept one parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 369.39,
          "end": 371.67,
          "en": "which typically is called props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 371.67,
          "end": 374.64,
          "en": "though, since it's your component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 374.64,
          "end": 377.76,
          "en": "you could name it anything you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 377.76,
          "end": 382.29,
          "en": "But since the overall React concept is called props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 382.29,
          "end": 386.283,
          "en": "this is the name that's typically chosen for this parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 387.51,
          "end": 391.83,
          "en": "Now this props parameter will be set by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 391.83,
          "end": 396.06,
          "en": "because it's React that will execute this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 396.06,
          "end": 398.67,
          "en": "Remember, you're not calling these component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 398.67,
          "end": 401.04,
          "en": "functions yourself in your code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 401.04,
          "end": 404.43,
          "en": "instead you're using them as html elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 404.43,
          "end": 408.483,
          "en": "And under the hood React will call the actual functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 409.32,
          "end": 414.27,
          "en": "Therefore, React will pass a value for this props parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 414.27,
          "end": 416.73,
          "en": "to this function when it calls it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 416.73,
          "end": 420.39,
          "en": "and the value that will be passed for this parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 420.39,
          "end": 424.23,
          "en": "to this function by React will be an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 424.23,
          "end": 429.23,
          "en": "and it will be an object that has all these key value pairs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 429.33,
          "end": 432.69,
          "en": "So all your custom attributes as keys",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 432.69,
          "end": 436.26,
          "en": "and the values for these attributes as values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 436.26,
          "end": 437.673,
          "en": "grouped into it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 438.69,
          "end": 442.23,
          "en": "So one object with these key value pairs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 442.23,
          "end": 445.443,
          "en": "that's what you'll get here for this props parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 447.12,
          "end": 449.52,
          "en": "And, therefore, in the component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 449.52,
          "end": 453.84000000000003,
          "en": "you can simply access props.image, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 453.84000000000003,
          "end": 457.623,
          "en": "to get hold of the value that's set on this image key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 458.7,
          "end": 461.13,
